Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||09-03-2001||10:27 PM||||There's a great, big world out there and at 17 you're just peeking out the door.  Enjoy what it has to offer.  Life is what you make of it.<P>Gary (old fart)<P>stupid llamas!||||reg||14
Z||000003||Formula88||09-03-2001||11:27 PM||||I agree with what you say, but have a few to add myself.<P>Love is giving the answer you know they don't want to hear, because you know they need to hear it.  It hurts you and them, but you do it because you love them.<P>Love is speaking no words at all and saying everything.<P>Love is not about fixing problems.  Love is a shelter you offer your loved ones so they can weather the storm.  You can't change the weather, but you can try to keep them dry till the rains pass.<P>Love is thinking about someone else before yourself.  (but <B><I>always</B></I> be true to yourself)<P>Love is what makes you alive.  It makes life worth living.  If you can't love, you're just existing.<P>Falling in love is taking a great risk of being hurt.  And the potential of that love being returned is worth - EVERY SINGLE TIME!<P>Love is blind, yes.  Wonderfully so.  I'm 36 years old and still love being infatuated.  I don't ever want to loose my romantic idealism. <P>Love is never easy.  Even in the best of relationships, there are problems.  It reminds me of Tom Hanks' description of baseball in "A League of Their Own," "It's not supposed to be easy.  If it were easy, everyone would do it.  It's the hard that makes it great."<P>That can be said of so many things in life.<P>You know what else love is?  Indescribeable.  And it's different each and every time.<P>[This message has been edited by Formula88 because he can't type worth a flip]<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||14
